---
const title = "EEG-based Attention Classification";
const description = "What does attention look like in EEG, and can you build a classifier around it?";
const tags = ["EEG", "Attention", "Machine Learning", "OpenBCI", "Signal Processing"];
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title} | seema rida</title>
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css" />
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #FAF8F5; --ink: #1C1917; --green: #4A7260; --green-mid: #D0E4DC;
      --muted: #78716C; --border: #E7E3DC; --card: #FFFFFF; --tag: #EEF4F1;
    }
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }

    nav { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 22px 52px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); position: sticky; top: 0; background: var(--bg); z-index: 100; }
    .nav-left { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
    .nav-left i { color: var(--green); font-size: 1.5rem; }
    .back-link { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.15s; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
    .back-link:hover { color: var(--ink); }

    .project-wrap { max-width: 100%; padding: 72px 15% 100px; }
    .project-header { margin-bottom: 48px; }
    .project-title { font-size: 3rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--ink); }
    .project-desc { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px; }

    .tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
    .tag { padding: 6px 14px; background: var(--tag); border: 1px solid var(--green-mid); border-radius: 100px; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); }

    .content { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.8; }
    .content h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 48px; margin-bottom: 20px; color: var(--ink); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .content h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
    .content h3 { font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--ink); }
    .content p { margin-bottom: 20px; color: var(--muted); }
    .content ul { margin-left: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; color: var(--muted); list-style-type: disc; }
    .content li { margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .content strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
    .content a { color: var(--green); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--green-mid); transition: border-color 0.15s; }
    .content a:hover { border-color: var(--green); }

    .research-question {
      background: var(--tag);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--green);
      padding: 24px;
      margin: 32px 0;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }
    .research-question p { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--ink); }

    .highlight-box {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 24px;
      margin: 32px 0;
    }
    .highlight-box p { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--muted); }

    .image-container {
      margin: 32px 0;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .image-container img {
      max-width: 100%;
      border-radius: 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .image-caption {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 12px;
      font-style: italic;
    }

    footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 32px 52px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; margin-top: 80px; }
    .fn { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted); }
    .fl { display: flex; gap: 26px; list-style: none; }
    .fl a { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.15s; }
    .fl a:hover { color: var(--ink); }

    @media (max-width: 1024px) {
      .project-wrap { padding: 60px 10% 80px; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .project-wrap { padding: 48px 8% 80px; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      nav { padding: 18px 20px; }
      .project-wrap { padding: 48px 6% 80px; }
      .project-title { font-size: 2rem; }
      footer { padding: 22px 20px; flex-direction: column; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <a href="/#research" class="back-link">← back to home</a>
  <div></div>
</nav>

<div class="project-wrap">
  <div class="project-header">
    <h1 class="project-title">{title}</h1>
    <div class="tags">
      {tags.map(tag => <span class="tag">{tag}</span>)}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content">
    <div class="research-question">
      <p>
        <strong>What does attention look like in EEG, and can you build a classifier around it?</strong>
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>The Motivation</h2>
    <p>
      The Pomodoro technique assumes everyone focuses on the same schedule. 25 minutes on, 5 minutes off, fixed, regardless of whether you're in flow or already checked out. It never really worked for me consistently and so I wanted to explore that.
    </p>

    <h2>The Experiment</h2>
    <p>
      Before building anything, we had to figure out what to actually measure. Eye movements artifact EEG badly, so a reading task was out. A listening task avoided that but couldn't capture visual attention.
    </p>
    <p>
      We landed on watching a lecture on a small screen. Participants watched for 10 minutes, took a 5-minute break, then another 10, while we recorded from 7 frontal channels using OpenBCI.
    </p>
    <p>
      They pressed keyboard buttons in real time to self-report when they lost focus and when they regained it.
    </p>

    <div class="image-container">
      <img src="/experiment.png" alt="Experimental setup" />
      <p class="image-caption">Experimental setup: participants watching lecture while wearing EEG headset</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Channels Used</h3>
    <p>
      All 7 channels sit in the frontal region. Fp1 and Fp2 cover the prefrontal cortex, most directly tied to attention and cognitive control. F3 and F4 capture working memory and focus, positioned symmetrically to pick up hemispheric differences. F7 and F8 track frontal asymmetry. Fz anchors the midline. Ground at O1, reference at O2.
    </p>

    <div class="image-container">
      <img src="/channels.png" alt="EEG channel placement" />
      <p class="image-caption">7 frontal channels used for attention detection</p>
    </div>

    <h2>What I Built</h2>
    <p>
      The pipeline filtered the raw EEG between 0.1 and 50 Hz, then epoched the data into 2-second windows aligned to the self-report markers. From each epoch I extracted relative band power across Delta, Theta, Alpha, Beta, and Gamma for all 7 channels.
    </p>
    <p>
      Alpha suppression and Beta elevation in frontal regions are established markers of active attention. Theta increases tend to signal cognitive load or fatigue.
    </p>

    <div class="image-container">
      <img src="/attention.png" alt="Attention detection visualization" />
      <p class="image-caption">Real-time attention state detection from EEG signals</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-container">
      <img src="/freq.png" alt="Frequency band analysis" />
      <p class="image-caption">Power spectral density across frequency bands during focused vs. unfocused states</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<footer>
